Configurable Docker ports + Account Settings page (v0.107)

Two independent changes:

1. Docker host ports (api/frontend/postgres) are now read from optional
   API_PORT/FRONTEND_PORT/POSTGRES_PORT env vars in docker-compose.yml
   instead of being hardcoded, defaulting to the same 8080/8081/5432 as
   before if unset. A machine that needs different host ports (a home
   server already running other services, say) now sets them in its own
   .env rather than hand-editing docker-compose.yml on every fresh
   install/update - see the new commented-out examples in .env.example.

2. "My Email" and "Customisation" (order status colours) - both always
   per-user settings under the hood (/users/me/settings) - moved out of
   Admin > Settings, where they sat alongside shared/global configuration,
   into a new Account Settings page reached via a settings icon next to
   your name at the bottom of the sidebar. The old "Log out" text link
   became an icon too, sitting next to it. SettingsSection (the
   collapsible-block component) was split out to its own file so both
   Settings.tsx and the new AccountSettings.tsx can share it.

